{
  "_comment": [
    "Tag configuration for Unit 1 and for collector health.",
    "Adding a tag is a row here, not an edit to Python (§341).",
    "ExcDev = CompDev/2 is the PI convention (§442).",
    "CompDev is set per tag on operational grounds; see _comp_dev_rationale.",
    "A CompDev below a tag's noise floor guarantees archiving noise. That is",
    "done deliberately for U1_BEARING_VIB, where the detail is worth the cost.",
    "RIG_* tags come from the bench rig via the Modbus bridge and live under the BenchRig object; source_path says so.",
    "Collector health tags are NOT listed here: they are generated from collector/health.py (HEALTH_MEASUREMENTS x INSTANCES) by collector/seed.py, so the tags and the code that publishes to them cannot drift apart. They carry the collector instance, so two collectors against the same archive are distinguishable (§455).",
    "compress: whether two-stage compression runs in the live path for this tag. Omitted means false, which keeps Stage 3's zero-loss measurement reproducible."
  ],
